<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Auto Backup and device-to-device transfer on API 31+. The API 28–30 half of
    the same rule lives in xml/backup_rules.xml; they must not drift.

    Both sections are allowlists: naming one <include> excludes everything not
    named, which is the point. The app's own preferences file carries a theme, a
    mask glyph and two reveal counts — nothing sensitive, and nothing that would
    embarrass a user restored onto a new phone. Nothing else the app writes
    leaves the device, so a card number cannot reach a cloud backup by way of a
    file somebody adds later.

    <device-transfer> gets the same allowlist rather than being left open. A
    direct phone-to-phone copy is a friendlier channel than Google's servers, but
    it is still a copy off this device, and there is nothing here worth widening
    the rule for.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <include domain="sharedpref" path="cardpro.xml" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <include domain="sharedpref" path="cardpro.xml" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
